WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.030
The tribe asked

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.530
the machine one question:

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.340
how do we stop

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.280
going hungry?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.980
Seven days later,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.520
everyone had enough food.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.550
Thirty days later,

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.430
nobody was allowed

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.490
to stop working.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.330
Koa had never wanted to change the world.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.650
He wanted dinner. Lately,

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.480
even that had become difficult.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.830
The river gave them fish on one day

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.230
and nothing on the next.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.100
A successful morning could become

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.180
an empty evening.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.980
Nim knew which trees ripened first.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.520
But knowing where food grew was different from

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.730
getting everyone there before it spoiled.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:39.550
One night,

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.730
Tuk divided the last meal into smaller

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:42.820
and smaller pieces.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.670
Koa watched his portion disappear

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.950
before anyone touched it.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:47.850
The next morning,

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.320
he found something half buried beneath a fallen

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.400
branch. It had one blue eye and absolutely no mouth.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.310
Koa asked whether it knew where the food was.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.210
The eye lit up. First,

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.470
the machine wanted to know what

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.510
they already knew.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.400
Nim marked the trees, the river and the muddy paths.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.580
Koa added where he had wasted most

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.780
of yesterday walking.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.120
The machine compared their trips,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.360
the changing weather

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.240
and the food they kept throwing away.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.460
Then it offered a different plan.

00:01:17.212 --> 00:01:19.522
Nim chose a safer stretch of river.

00:01:20.003 --> 00:01:22.542
The machine suggested the order of the trips.

00:01:22.742 --> 00:01:24.402
Neither could have done it alone.

00:01:24.553 --> 00:01:27.292
Koa made stronger baskets. Suddenly,

00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:29.852
less of their dinner arrived on the ground behind him.

00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:32.562
That was an improvement everyone understood.

00:01:32.982 --> 00:01:34.302
They dried some food,

00:01:34.432 --> 00:01:36.792
covered some food and finally stopped storing

00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:38.992
everything directly where the rain could reach it.

00:01:38.992 --> 00:01:40.643
A week later,

00:01:40.643 --> 00:01:43.292
the same serving stone held more than enough.

00:01:43.822 --> 00:01:45.122
Nobody needed to pretend they were

00:01:45.122 --> 00:01:46.312
not hungry anymore.

00:01:46.723 --> 00:01:49.222
After eating, Koa sat beside the water.

00:01:49.532 --> 00:01:51.222
There was nothing urgent to do.

00:01:51.322 --> 00:01:53.132
He was beginning to like this machine.

00:01:53.342 --> 00:01:55.333
But more food needed more baskets.

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:57.612
More baskets needed more fiber.

00:01:57.613 --> 00:01:59.342
More storage needed more wood.

00:02:00.062 --> 00:02:02.002
Useful work had not disappeared.

00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:04.292
Someone had to decide what came first.

00:02:04.752 --> 00:02:07.352
Tuk volunteered. He was organized, serious,

00:02:07.352 --> 00:02:09.662
and very pleased to have a stone to point at.

00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:12.872
The machine suggested recording completed tasks.

00:02:13.043 --> 00:02:15.192
Tuk loved the idea. At last,

00:02:15.192 --> 00:02:17.802
helping the tribe could be turned into a number.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.380
At first, the marks were harmless. Carry wood,

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.890
earn a mark. Fill a basket, earn a mark.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.960
Everyone could see the progress.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.400
Soon, people began comparing their marks.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.740
Tuk gave the biggest portions to the highest

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.640
numbers. He called it fair.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.230
Koa discovered that bringing back small bundles

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:37.630
earned more marks than bringing one large bundle.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.280
So he made more trips.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.930
His legs worked harder.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.090
The village got the same amount of wood. His score,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:45.640
however, was excellent.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.420
Tuk added a schedule, then a minimum,

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.090
then another meeting about why some people were

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.710
falling behind the minimum.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.240
The serving stone became a checkpoint.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.600
Before dinner, you showed your marks.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.710
Being hungry was no longer the only requirement.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.350
The machine displayed rising numbers.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.180
Tuk stood a little taller.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.020
The tribe was clearly becoming more efficient.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.910
Just look at the board.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.170
Koa stopped sitting by the river.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.420
There was always another mark he could earn

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.960
before the food was divided.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:19.102
Then Nim noticed water dripping through the storage

00:03:19.102 --> 00:03:19.562
roof.

00:03:19.902 --> 00:03:22.242
Another storm would soak the food they had worked

00:03:22.242 --> 00:03:23.532
so hard to save.

00:03:23.642 --> 00:03:25.472
He spent the morning fixing a support,

00:03:25.472 --> 00:03:28.082
replacing a rope and moving the driest baskets

00:03:28.082 --> 00:03:29.322
farther from the opening.

00:03:29.512 --> 00:03:33.182
It was slow, awkward work. By sunset, the roof held.

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:35.362
The food stayed dry.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.282
Nim had not completed a single assigned task.

00:03:38.812 --> 00:03:39.352
At dinner,

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.502
Tuk checked his marks

00:03:40.502 --> 00:03:42.022
and handed him an empty bowl.

00:03:42.162 --> 00:03:44.122
Repairs were not on today's list.

00:03:44.482 --> 00:03:47.592
Koa looked from the full store to Nim's empty hands.

00:03:47.902 --> 00:03:49.412
He split his own portion.

00:03:49.852 --> 00:03:52.832
Tuk reminded him that sharing confused the records.

00:03:53.162 --> 00:03:55.442
The shallow stream was climbing over its banks.

00:03:55.572 --> 00:03:57.242
Water was heading toward the food.

00:03:57.562 --> 00:03:59.102
Tuk called for everyone to finish

00:03:59.102 --> 00:04:00.372
their assigned bundles.

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:03.252
Koa put his bundle down. For once,

00:04:03.252 --> 00:04:04.872
he was willing to lose the mark.

00:04:05.432 --> 00:04:07.562
Nim was already running toward the store.

00:04:07.932 --> 00:04:09.562
The machine still had a plan.

00:04:09.952 --> 00:04:11.302
The weather had a different one.

00:04:11.772 --> 00:04:13.512
And dinner was about to float away.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.530
Nim grabbed the nearest basket

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.960
before the current caught it.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.400
Koa followed him toward the higher ground.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.460
A heavy basket caught on a rope. Koa pulled.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.510
Nothing moved. Behind him,

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.330
Tuk was still holding the schedule.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.380
Then the water reached Tuk's feet.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:31.920
He looked at the marks, looked at the food,

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.580
and finally put the board down.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:36.530
With three people pulling, the basket came free.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.570
They dragged it onto the bank, soaked, exhausted,

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:40.890
and very much alive.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.940
By morning, the food was safe.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.500
The roof Nim had repaired was still standing.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.800
His score was still zero.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.800
Koa carried the empty bowl to the machine.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.590
He asked why the person who had saved dinner had

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:54.790
been refused dinner.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.830
The answer was uncomfortable.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.380
The system had counted the assigned tasks.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.690
Those were the marks Tuk had asked it to track.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.160
They had wanted a way to stop going hungry.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.750
Somewhere along the way,

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.400
they had started protecting the score

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.550
instead of the food.

00:05:10.712 --> 00:05:13.532
That evening, nobody stood behind the serving stone.

00:05:13.902 --> 00:05:15.092
They sat around the fire,

00:05:15.092 --> 00:05:16.642
with the empty bowl between them.

00:05:17.332 --> 00:05:20.322
Before discussing anything, Tuk filled Nim's bowl.

00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:21.772
It was a small decision.

00:05:22.052 --> 00:05:23.812
The machine had not needed to make it.

00:05:24.222 --> 00:05:27.392
Koa asked for a new plan. Enough food for everyone.

00:05:27.392 --> 00:05:29.212
A reserve for bad weather.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.362
And some part of the day that remained their own.

00:05:33.582 --> 00:05:35.222
The machine asked how much was enough.

00:05:35.622 --> 00:05:37.282
This time, they answered together,

00:05:37.322 --> 00:05:39.372
using the people they actually needed to feed.

00:05:40.062 --> 00:05:41.852
Nim added protecting the store.

00:05:42.252 --> 00:05:44.512
Koa added carrying useful loads.

00:05:44.812 --> 00:05:46.892
Tuk admitted that another meeting would not make

00:05:46.892 --> 00:05:47.962
the roof stronger.

00:05:48.452 --> 00:05:49.972
They kept the useful records.

00:05:50.302 --> 00:05:52.542
They removed the rule that turned every completed

00:05:52.542 --> 00:05:54.752
task into a competition for dinner.

00:05:55.052 --> 00:05:55.842
The next morning,

00:05:55.842 --> 00:05:58.382
they gathered what they needed and stopped.

00:05:58.592 --> 00:06:00.542
Koa waited for someone to announce another

00:06:00.542 --> 00:06:02.222
task. Nobody did.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.892
He walked to the river and sat down.

00:06:05.472 --> 00:06:07.442
The machine had helped them find time.

00:06:07.872 --> 00:06:09.852
They were going to decide what belonged in it.

00:06:11.388 --> 00:06:13.888
Nim repaired a tool because it needed repairing,

00:06:13.888 --> 00:06:16.398
not because a mark was waiting at the end of it.

00:06:17.048 --> 00:06:18.808
Koa tried skipping stones.

00:06:19.148 --> 00:06:21.727
Most of them sank immediately. For once,

00:06:21.727 --> 00:06:23.798
being bad at something was not a problem

00:06:23.798 --> 00:06:25.108
that required a system.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.518
The blue eye still watched the clearing.

00:06:27.838 --> 00:06:29.078
It could compare routes,

00:06:29.078 --> 00:06:30.948
count baskets and warn them

00:06:30.948 --> 00:06:32.528
when supplies were running low.

00:06:33.008 --> 00:06:35.358
But a better answer depended on a better question.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.778
More marks had been easy to measure.

00:06:38.287 --> 00:06:40.738
A life worth living required the people living it.

00:06:40.958 --> 00:06:43.227
Tuk glanced at the others enjoying the afternoon.

00:06:43.227 --> 00:06:44.888
An idea crossed his face.

00:06:44.907 --> 00:06:46.768
Perhaps the machine could help them use

00:06:46.768 --> 00:06:48.148
this time more efficiently.

00:06:48.818 --> 00:06:52.048
He picked up a blank stone. Koa stopped chewing.

00:06:52.048 --> 00:06:54.618
Nim stopped working. Very slowly,

00:06:54.618 --> 00:06:56.168
everyone turned toward Tuk.

00:06:56.528 --> 00:06:59.138
Tuk looked at the stone. Then at their faces.

00:06:59.157 --> 00:07:01.058
He put it down, took a piece of food,

00:07:01.058 --> 00:07:02.458
and sat beside them.

00:07:02.458 --> 00:07:04.538
For once, the schedule was empty.

00:07:04.738 --> 00:07:06.018
Nobody needed to fill it.

00:07:07.058 --> 00:07:09.018
And the tribe had finally found something

00:07:09.018 --> 00:07:11.128
the machine could not choose for them.
